# State Management Rules

## Ownership

```text
SERVER STATE   -> TanStack Query  (packages/api query/mutations)
CLIENT/UI STATE -> Redux Toolkit   (packages/state)
```

Do **not** put API response data into Redux unless there is a very specific, documented reason
(ADR or `docs/ops/WORKER.md` note).

## TanStack Query owns

Fetching, caching, stale state, refetching, retries, pagination, infinite queries, mutation
lifecycle, optimistic updates where appropriate, server-state synchronization.

## Redux Toolkit may own

Session/client state, current workspace, selected organization, global preferences,
application-level UI state, cross-route workflows, persisted client preferences.

## MUST NOT enter Redux

- Server/remote data owned by TanStack Query
- Derived data computable from queries/selectors
- Ephemeral local component state that never crosses routes
- Secrets/tokens in plain persisted state (use secure auth adapters)

## Agent rules

- Prefer Query hooks from `@azes/api` for remote data.
- Prefer RTK slices from `@azes/state` only for justified client/global state.
- Do not invent a second cache of the same server data in Redux.
- For API/QueryClient/auth-bridge runtime work, follow `.cursor/rules/apiMenecerAgent.mdc`
  and keep `docs/api/CURRENT-STATE.md` current.

See `docs/architecture/state-architecture.md` and `docs/decisions/ADR-002-state-management.md`.
